The equation of motion of a projectile is $y=a x-b x^2$, where $a, b$ are constants. Match the column - I with column - II
$\begin{array}{ll}
\text{Column - I} &amp; \text{Column - II} \\
\text{i) The initial velocity of projection} &amp; \text{a)} \frac{a}{b} \\
\text{ii) The horizontal range of projectile} &amp; \text{b)} a \sqrt{\frac{2}{\mathrm{bg}}} \\
\text{iii) The maximum height attained by projectile} &amp; \text{c)} \frac{\mathrm{a}^2}{4 \mathrm{~b}} \\
\text{iv) The time of flight of projectile} &amp; \text{d)} \sqrt{\frac{g\left(1+a^2\right)}{2 b}}
\end{array}

